# What Cloudflare Workers actually deploys as static assets — everything
# else in the repo root is excluded here, gitignore-style syntax. This
# file is what fixes the "Asset too large" build failure: without it,
# Wrangler bundles the ENTIRE repo root (assets.directory in
# wrangler.jsonc is "." — has to be, see that file's comment for why),
# which once `npm install` runs during Cloudflare's build includes
# node_modules — and wrangler's own dependency, workerd, ships a 127MB
# binary, well past the Workers 25MB-per-file limit.
#
# Runtime-required, deliberately NOT excluded below: index.html (the root
# redirect stub), Public/, JS/, CSS/, sw.js (the root-scoped Service
# Worker — see JS/main.js's registration comment for why it has to live
# at the root and not inside Public/).

# The actual blocker — a Cloudflare/npm build artifact, never committed,
# but present in Cloudflare's own build sandbox by the time Wrangler runs.
node_modules

# Everything below is real, committed, and fine to keep in git — just
# none of it is something a browser ever fetches, so none of it belongs
# on the public CDN either.
.git
.github
.vscode
Supabase
db-tests
test
package.json
package-lock.json
README.md
.gitignore
.gitattributes
gen_sounds.py
*.patch
proximity-scanner-remarks-instructions.md
wrangler.jsonc
.assetsignore